KZ3 patch 2084: LD_POST_WB_DIAG, which SPU DMA reads of a live RSX surface saw the RSX's last write (pass 78).

KZ3 runs its post chain (MLAA, bloom, DoF, motion blur, vignette, grain) on the SPUs over render targets the RSX
drew in main memory; patch 2017 writes those back at guest sync points (semaphore release, flip). This diagnostic
tells per surface record and report window whether each SPU GET that overlapped it read written-back bytes
(fresh), bytes the GPU had overwritten since the last write-back (stale), bytes of a record never written back
(never), or a record the GPU never drew to (nogpu). Local-memory surfaces are counted too (2017's sync write-back
covers main memory only).

- runtime/spu: g_spu_guest_read_hook + spu_set_guest_read_hook (spu_coherency.c), called on every DMA GET
  (spu_dma.h) when non-null; null unless LD_POST_WB_DIAG > 0, so the default path only tests one pointer.
- cellGcmSys.c: gcm_spu_read_ea (EA -> location/offset, per 1 MB IO page, as gcm_note_pages_ea) installed with
  the write hook when LD_POST_WB_DIAG > 0.
- rsx_live_draw.c: rsx_live_draw_note_spu_read; per-record GPU-write / write-back counters at
  ld_gv_note_gpu_write and both write-back paths; ld_pwd_flip prints one `[post-wb]` line per record with SPU
  GETs every N frames (LD_POST_WB_DIAG=N, 1 = 60; at most 4000 lines).
